config SENSEI_SECURE
	bool "SENSEI end-to-end envelope (ECDH P-256, HKDF, AES-128-GCM)"
	depends on SENSEI
	select SENSEI_CRYPTO
	select SENSEI_CRYPTO_AEAD
	select SENSEI_CRYPTO_ECDH
	select SENSEI_CRYPTO_HKDF
	help
	  Envelope library on the SENSEI SDK crypto library (lib/sensei_secure/README.md).

config SENSEI_SECURE_RATCHET
	bool "Forward secrecy: root key, mix and uplink chain (X25519, HMAC-SHA256)"
	default y
	depends on SENSEI_SECURE
	select SENSEI_CRYPTO_HMAC
	select SENSEI_CRYPTO_X25519
	help
	  lib/sensei_secure/src/sensei_ratchet.c and the X25519, HMAC functions of the cipher backend. The envelope itself
	  reads generation 1 and later (the ratchet bits of the kind byte) with or without this option, but needs a keyring
	  for it (struct sensei_secure_keyring). Without it about 1 kB of flash less, and the node cannot mix.

config SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS
	bool "Keep the end-to-end keys and counters in the settings subsystem"
	depends on SENSEI_SECURE
	select SETTINGS
	help
	  Storage backend of sensei_e2e (sensei_e2e_settings.h): key pair, collector key, counters.

config SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_PREFIX
	string "Settings key prefix"
	default "sensei_comm"
	depends on SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS
	help
	  The keys are <prefix>/e2e_priv (e2e_privx when sealed), e2e_bpub, e2e_tx, e2e_rxs and e2e_rxf. The default is the prefix
	  of the SENSEI IEQ node: a node that updates keeps its keys. Changing it makes stored keys
	  unreachable (a new key pair is made, the collector has to be provisioned again).

config SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_SEAL
	bool "Seal the secret records of the key store (AES-128-GCM)"
	depends on SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS
	help
	  The private key is stored as e2e_privx, a sealed record (sensei_e2e_seal.h: version, nonce, AES-128-GCM
	  ciphertext, tag), not as plain e2e_priv. A plain e2e_priv of an earlier version is migrated at the first
	  start: sealed, read back and checked. The plain record stays until the application calls
	  sensei_e2e_settings_confirm() after it has confirmed the image (a trial image that MCUboot reverts finds its
	  key); a plain record that is not a valid key is not sealed, the key store replaces it. The key comes from the function
	  sensei_e2e_settings_seal_key() (sensei_e2e_settings.h): one of the providers below, or the application's
	  own. If the key is not available, or a sealed record does not open, the key store does not start
	  (sensei_e2e_init() fails) and no new key pair is made over the old one. The name e2e_rat is reserved for
	  the ratchet state of a later version.

if SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_SEAL

config SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_SEAL_HUK
	bool "Key from the hardware unique key (CryptoCell-312 and KMU of the nRF5340)"
	depends on HAS_HW_NRF_CC312 && HW_UNIQUE_KEY_SUPPORTED && NRF_CC3XX_PLATFORM && !BUILD_WITH_TFM
	depends on !SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_SEAL_TEST_KEY
	select HW_UNIQUE_KEY
	select HW_UNIQUE_KEY_RANDOM
	select MPU_ALLOW_FLASH_WRITE
	help
	  zephyr/sensei_e2e_huk.c: at the first use a random hardware unique key is written to the KMU (once, until
	  the chip is erased; the CPU cannot read it), and the sealing key is derived from it with the label
	  "SENSEI-E2E-AT-REST-v1". A flash image copied to another chip does not open, and stale settings pages
	  are unreadable without code execution on the chip. The debug port must still be locked (APPROTECT).
	  Needs NRF_CC3XX_PLATFORM (the application enables it; the CryptoCell also provides the random numbers).

config SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_SEAL_TEST_KEY
	bool "Fixed key for tests (native_sim)"
	help
	  zephyr/sensei_e2e_testkey.c: a fixed key that a test can change or make fail. Never for a product: the
	  key is in the image.

endif # SENSEI_SECURE_SETTINGS_SEAL
